  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strong: every thermal incident reported to the regulator within 24 hours, all-scope, with 48-hour customer notice. S2 keeps the 5% limit and gives numeric per-model results to purchasers and regulators (not the public), but softens enforcement with a 36-month transition lacking any interim cap and no automatic sales stop. S3 and S4 satisfy the companies' red lines (6-year retrofit, 36-month suppression), though S3's 24-month new-unit deadline is loose; S5 retains the mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with only 'prompt' notices and no serious-injury clause."
